# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vidnov × Postiz — environment TEMPLATE (key names only, no real secrets).
#
# On the VPS:   cd /root/postiz && cp env.template .env && nano .env
# Generate secrets with (never reuse Vidnov values):
#   openssl rand -base64 48 | tr -d '\n'      # → POSTIZ_JWT_SECRET
#   openssl rand -base64 32 | tr -d '\n'      # → POSTIZ_PG_PASSWORD
#   openssl rand -base64 32 | tr -d '\n'      # → TEMPORAL_PG_PASSWORD
#
# NEVER put Vidnov/Firebase/PocketBase/Resend secrets in this file.
# NEVER commit a filled .env (it is gitignored — see .gitignore).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Required: instance secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────
POSTIZ_JWT_SECRET=<generate-48-byte-random>
POSTIZ_PG_PASSWORD=<generate-32-byte-random>
TEMPORAL_PG_PASSWORD=<generate-32-byte-random>

# ── Required: database names ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
POSTIZ_PG_USER=postiz
POSTIZ_PG_DB=vidnov_postiz

# ── Required: registration gate ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# FIRST RUN ONLY: set to false to create the owner account, then set back to
# true and run `docker compose up -d --force-recreate postiz` (README step 8).
POSTIZ_DISABLE_REGISTRATION=false

# ── Optional: public API limit (posts per hour) ──────────────────────────────
POSTIZ_API_LIMIT=30

# ── Optional: Postiz transactional email (activation notices) ────────────────
# Names only — either leave unset (accounts auto-activate) or set your Resend
# key here if you want Postiz to send its own activation emails. This does NOT
# change any Vidnov DNS/email records.
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend
# RESEND_API_KEY=<only-if-you-choose-to-enable-postiz-email>

# ── Optional: object storage instead of the local uploads volume ─────────────
# STORAGE_PROVIDER is set to `local` in docker-compose.yml; if you switch it to
# `cloudflare` there, fill these (see docs.postiz.com/self-host/configuration/reference):
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCESS_KEY=
# CLOUDFLARE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# CLOUDFLARE_BUCKETNAME=
# CLOUDFLARE_BUCKET_URL=
# CLOUDFLARE_REGION=auto

# ── Social platform credentials (fill ONLY what you legitimately own) ────────
# Leave blank until you create/obtain each provider app. Key names below match
# the official Postiz configuration reference:
# https://docs.postiz.com/self-host/configuration/reference
#
# Zero-developer-app channels (Bluesky, Telegram, Medium, Dev.to, Hashnode,
# WordPress, …) need NO keys here — they are connected inside the Postiz UI.
# See CHANNELS.md.
#
# X_API_KEY=
# X_API_SECRET=
# LINKEDIN_CLIENT_ID=
# LINKEDIN_CLIENT_SECRET=
# FACEBOOK_APP_ID=
# FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET=
# THREADS_APP_ID=
# THREADS_APP_SECRET=
# YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=
# YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# TIKTOK_CLIENT_ID=
# TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET=
# PINTEREST_CLIENT_ID=
# REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
# REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=
# DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=
# DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=
# DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN_ID=
# MASTODON_URL=https://mastodon.social
# MASTODON_CLIENT_ID=
# MASTODON_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# Do NOT set any Stripe keys — this install has no billing (AGPL self-host).
# Do NOT set OPENAI_API_KEY unless you deliberately want Postiz AI features.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vidnov → Postiz integration keys (READ BY VIDNOV'S SERVER, NOT BY COMPOSE)
# Create the API key inside Postiz (Settings → API keys) after first login,
# then put it in Vidnov's server environment (never NEXT_PUBLIC_*):
#   POSTIZ_API_URL=https://social.vidnov.com
#   POSTIZ_API_KEY=<created-in-postiz-ui>
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
